use ../knowledge/summary-knowledge.flow
use ../knowledge/common-knowledge.flow
use ../knowledge/draft-knowledge.flow

do Resolve the explicit project or current checkout and active ticket from
    @request or conversation. Reject supplied-ID mismatches. Return an object
    with project, ticket_id (null if unknown), and ticket (complete matching
    cached Jira object or null). as @task_context

if @task_context.ticket_id == null
    ask "Which Jira ticket should this work use?" as @ticket_input
    do Validate @ticket_input against the active task and return @task_context
        updated with that one Jira ID. as @task_context

set project = @task_context.project
set ticket_id = @task_context.ticket_id
set ticket = @task_context.ticket

do Retain the verified project, ticket ID, and any complete cached ticket as
    this conversation's active task without remote calls or task files.

do Resolve and read the pr.md draft for @project and @ticket_id under
    @draft_rules. Require an existing selected draft.
    Return an object with path and text. as @draft_state

set draft_path = @draft_state.path
set saved_draft = @draft_state.text

do Read applicable project AGENTS.md and explicit user naming overrides.
    Current rules take precedence over old conversation conventions. as @project_rules

do Use @ticket and @saved_draft. Return an object with saved_pr and the exact
    unrequested sections that must be preserved. as @documents

do Check branch and HEAD in @project before reusing implementation evidence. Inspect
    committed changes only for material gaps. Do not fetch, choose a target, or
    run a readiness pass. Return the evidence and observed checks. as @evidence

do Build an in-memory draft from @documents.saved_pr, @request, @evidence,
    @writing_guidance, and @summary_rules. Refine only the requested Title line
    or Description. Preserve accurate notes and unrequested sections
    byte-for-byte. Return an object with draft and unrelated_gaps. as @refinement

do Save and verify @refinement.draft only to @draft_path under @draft_rules, using
    @saved_draft as the concurrent-edit baseline. Verify the active project and
    ticket still match @project and @ticket_id.

print Report @draft_path, @evidence, and @refinement.unrelated_gaps briefly.
